   "note": {
    "en": "The standing name of the majority school, not a description assembled on the spot — which is why the three words are read as one term. Grammatically nothing is suspended: أَهْلِ is a mudaf, السُّنَّةِ its mudaf ilayh, and وَالْجَمَاعَةِ is coupled to السُّنَّةِ in jarr.",
